npc :nadya_tsoi do
  name "Nadya Tsoi"
  tags :military, :catastrophe, :autonomy
  prominence :marginal

  prose <<~PROSE
    A contract scout on #{ref :tangwang_post, "Tangwang Post"}'s roll, from a Bureya-bank family that has put scouts on the #{ref :the_amur_line, "line"} since the campaigns. She walks a compartment and the two kilometres beyond it. Her mark decides where crews make the next of #{ref :the_dead_rings, "the dead rings"}.

    She carries a brass compass, a watch, a glass soil thermometer, a knife, a pencil and paper. Nothing she carries reports and nothing she wears is alive. Her hut stands outside the post's #{ref :continental_mycelium, "fungal growth"}. This gives the post one observer whose first reading comes from her own instruments at the tree line.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :operations, heading: "How She Walks"
    Tsoi stops at the edge of a compartment before entering and listens for a hundred breaths. She records each thing in the order she meets it, with paces in the left margin and nothing moved later even where the ninth observation explains the third. The first line is nearly always a sound or its absence.

    On the Compartment Twelve walk her first line was quiet at the north edge: no thrush, no siskin. Below it she recorded roe deer beds on north aspects at three hundred and forty paces, litter at 100 millimetres reading 3.4 degrees above the shaded air at the same hour, and #{ref :sanchakou, "Sanchakou"}'s hazel row leafed a week ahead of the coppice behind it. Her sheet treats the warm litter as one observation among the silent birds, displaced deer and early leaves; the combined change is what she marked.
  PROSE

  prose <<~PROSE, section: :people, heading: "Compartment Twelve"
    Tsoi marked #{ref :the_sanchakou_ring, "Compartment Twelve"} despite #{ref :xie_lanting, "Xie Lanting"}'s cores, which found foreign growth in two trees where the local threshold was four. Silent birds, displaced deer, warm litter and early leaves outweighed the wood in her decision.

    In the same week she allowed Xie to cut sixty dormant scions from Sanchakou's orchard before the trees were killed. #{ref :continuity, "Continuity"} objected to the living wood leaving the compartment, not to the dead ring.
  PROSE

  log "2026-08-09 — The walk sheet is a water-well driller's strata log, a trade nobody on the reach practises: strata are entered in the order the bit meets them, with thickness against each, and never reordered once a lower stratum explains an upper one. That fixed both the order of the sheet and the unit in the margin — paces, because a scout's only measure of thickness is how far she walked through it."
end
